<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="z1-configuration">
    <title>Configuration Guide</title>
    <shortdesc>This guide explains how to configure and activate the Z1 Encryption Server after
        installation.</shortdesc>
    <body>
        <section id="section_zbg_4tn_dhc">
            <title>Accessing the Configuration Interface</title>
            <p>
                <?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron" comment="Consider removing &apos;the&apos; before &apos;installation&apos; for conciseness: &apos;After installation, open your web browser...&apos;."?>After
                the installation, open your web browser and access the Z1 Administration Interface
                using the following URL:<?oxy_comment_end?>
            </p>
            <codeblock id="codeblock_acg_4tn_dhc">https://localhost:8443</codeblock>
            <p>
                <?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron" comment="For clarity, consider specifying &apos;administrator credentials that you created during setup.&apos; Also, consider splitting the second sentence for readability: &apos;If you are accessing the interface remotely, ensure that port 8443 is open on your firewall.&apos;."?>Log
                in with your administrator credentials created during setup. If you are accessing
                the interface remotely, ensure that port <codeph>8443</codeph> is open in your
                firewall.<?oxy_comment_end?>
            </p>
        </section>
        <section id="section_bcg_4tn_dhc">
            <title>Setting Up Encryption Keys</title>
            <p>
                <?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron" comment="Consider rephrasing for clarity: &apos;Encryption keys are essential for securing communications.&apos; (plural) and &apos;Follow these steps to generate and store keys:&apos;."?>Encryption
                keys are essential for securing communication. Follow these steps to generate and
                store your keys:<?oxy_comment_end?>
            </p>
            <ol id="ol_ccg_4tn_dhc">
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron"?>In the Administration Interface,
                    navigate to <u>Security</u> → <u>Key Management</u>.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron"?>Click <b>Generate New Key</b> and
                    choose the key type (RSA or ECC).<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron" comment="Consider rephrasing for parallel structure: &apos;Select the key length (2048 or 4096 bits) and assign a descriptive name to the key.&apos;."?>Select
                    the key length (2048 or 4096 bits) and assign a descriptive
                    name.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron"?>Click <b>Save</b> to store the key
                    securely in the local keystore.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
            </ol>
        </section>
        <section id="section_dcg_4tn_dhc">
            <title>Connecting to the Directory Service</title>
            <p>
                <?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron" comment="Consider rephrasing for clarity: &apos;To enable automatic certificate lookup and user management, integrate Z1 with your directory service as follows:&apos;."?>To
                enable automatic certificate lookup and user management, integrate Z1 with your
                directory service:<?oxy_comment_end?>
            </p>
            <ol id="ol_ecg_4tn_dhc">
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron"?>Go to <u>Configuration</u> →
                        <u>Directory Settings</u>.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron"?>Select your service type: <b>Active
                        Directory</b> or <b>LDAP</b>.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron" comment="Consider specifying: &apos;Enter the directory server address, port number, and authentication credentials.&apos;."?>Enter
                    the server address, port number, and authentication
                    credentials.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
                <li><?oxy_comment_start author="AI Positron"?>Click <b>Test Connection</b> to verify
                    connectivity.<?oxy_comment_end?></li>
            </ol>
        </section>
    </body>
</topic>
